---
// Was jaan.li/glucose.
import Viz from "../../layouts/Viz.astro";
import VizEmbed from "../../components/VizEmbed.astro";
---

<Viz
  title="Millions of glucose levels"
  description="Blood glucose readings across 300,000 hospitalizations of 150,000 people, cross-filtered against the diagnostic category each patient was admitted under."
  eyebrow="Visualizations"
  eyebrowHref="/visualizations"
>
  <p class="viz-note">
    The two views are linked. Select bars in the diagnostic-category chart to filter the heatmap and
    isolate the pattern for those admissions; or drag a rectangle in the heatmap to show only the
    categories that fall inside it. Both queries run in your browser, against the full table, as you
    drag.
  </p>

  {
    /* Laid out at a fixed 1063px and given its own scroller. Mosaic sizes a
       plot when it is constructed and these two share a live selection, so
       re-rendering on resize would throw away whatever the reader had brushed.
       See viz/src/charts/glucose.js. */
  }
  <VizEmbed module="glucose" export="GlucoseCrossfilter" minHeight={880} scroll />

  <p class="viz-note">
    The time axis runs from 2105 to 2214. That is not an error: MIMIC-IV shifts every patient's
    dates forward into the 2100s by a random per-patient offset, which preserves the intervals
    within a single stay — the thing the heatmap is actually about — while severing any connection
    to a real calendar date.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="sources">
    <ul>
      <li>Data: MIMIC-IV, a de-identified critical care database.</li>
      <li>
        Transform: <a
          href="https://github.com/jaanli/mimic-iv-visualization/blob/89af4215cc1f77da1918e991f1447a175ade8117/data_processing/models/figures/glucose_full.sql"
          rel="noopener">glucose_full.sql</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</Viz>
